## Interface: 11509, 50504
# THE FIRST LINE OF THE FILE, AND IT HAS TO BE.
#
# This sat at line 12, behind the comment block now below it, and the Mists
# client refused the addon outright - GetAddOnInfo reported
# `loadable=false, reason=INTERFACE_VERSION` while the .toc plainly declared
# 50504 and the client plainly was 50504. AetherProbe, byte-identical on this
# line but carrying it as line 1, loaded fine beside it.
#
# Era never showed it: that install has `checkAddonVersion "0"` set, so nothing
# is ever refused for its interface version and a .toc the client could not read
# looked perfectly healthy for a day.
#
# TWO CLIENTS, ONE FILE. 11509 is Classic Era 1.15.9; 50504 is Mists of
# Pandaria Classic 5.5.0.4 - 50504 rather than the 50500 the expansion suggests,
# because the client is 5.5.0.4 and that is what every shipping MoP addon
# declares.
#
# ONE TOC RATHER THAN AetherUI_Vanilla.toc + AetherUI_Mists.toc. Both spellings
# work and both are in live use, but the split one writes the VERSION down twice
# and Tools/bump.py is the only thing allowed to write it. A version that has to
# be typed into two files is a version that will be wrong in one of them. Split
# it the day the two flavours need different FILE LISTS, and not before -
# everything flavour-specific so far branches inside Lua on A.isMists.
## Title: Aether|cff9d7bffUI|r
## Notes: A frosted-glass HUD for Classic Era and Mists of Pandaria Classic.
## Author: DrVeoj
## Version: 1.0.0
## SavedVariables: AetherUIDB
## X-Category: Interface Enhancements
# THE ICON IN THE ADDON LIST. Blizzard_AddOnList reads this and prepends it to
# the title as a 20x20 inline texture; set neither this nor IconAtlas and you
# get the yellow question mark that every unlabelled addon wears.
#
# NO FILE EXTENSION, and the path is spelled out rather than built. The .toc is
# read before a line of this addon's Lua runs, so Media.texture.icon does not
# exist yet to be asked - which makes this the second place that path is
# written down, and the harness checks the two still agree.
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\AetherUI\Media\Textures\Icon
# The CurseForge project. The packager needs this to upload at all, and
# needs it again to resolve the @localization@ blocks in Locale/ - a key
# without an id substitutes nothing.
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1666829
# Wago Addons. Its id is a short string rather than a number, and it is not a
# slug you can guess - it comes off the project page.
## X-Wago-ID: EGPegON1

